FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] tests/doc_blocks_test.rs:578 — RUNS now requires `rb compile` to exit 0 but `compile_block` (tests/doc_blocks_test.rs:275) never runs the emitted `.rbc`, so a literal lowering that compiles to the wrong closure still passes the doc gate — concrete fix: after a successful compile, run `rb vm` on the artifact and require exit 0 plus identical stdout to `rb run`.
2. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/codegen.rs:807 — `Expr::FunctionLiteral` builds its `Decl` with `span: Span::unknown()` while every statement-level `Decl` (e.g. src/bytecode/codegen.rs:438 uses `stmt.span`), so a block-depth refusal inside a literal loses its line/column — concrete fix: carry the literal's source line into the `Span` instead of `unknown`.
3. [MINOR] tests/function_literal_test.rs:703 — `both_fail` asserts only `message()` equality while the equivalent `both_errors` in tests/method_map_test.rs:99 asserts `label()` and `message()`, so a Runtime-vs-Limit divergence with identical text passes here — concrete fix: assert `label()` equality too, as the map helper does.
